http://loinc.org/license. LOINC® is a registered United States trademark of
Regenstrief Institute, Inc.

Source: LOINC release 2.83, its zh-CN linguistic variant
(AccessoryFiles/LinguisticVariants/zhCN5LinguisticVariant.csv, variant ID 5,
produced by Lin Zhang, a LOINC volunteer from China), Loinc.csv,
AccessoryFiles/ConsumerName/ConsumerName.csv and AccessoryFiles/PartFile/Part.csv.

What these files are:

  zh_CN_parts.tsv.gz  The six Parts (COMPONENT, PROPERTY, TIME_ASPCT, SYSTEM,
                      SCALE_TYP, METHOD_TYP) of every code in
                      fhir_loinc_bundle.tar.gz that the zh-CN variant covers.
                      Parts used by the codes LOINC ranks as commonly ordered
                      (COMMON_TEST_RANK) were reviewed one by one against the
                      variant and corrected where the variant was wrong, stale
                      against the current English Part, or not the standard
                      Chinese term; every other Part is the variant's text,
                      unchanged. standardize_build/zh_CN/parts.tsv lists each
                      reviewed Part beside the variant's rendering. A last
                      column holds the Chinese consumer name where the code's
                      English ConsumerName is one translated for a commonly
                      ordered code.
  zh_CN_names.tsv     LONG_COMMON_NAME and LinguisticVariantDisplayName in
                      Chinese for those commonly ordered codes. The zh-CN
                      variant leaves both columns empty.
  en_parts.tsv.gz     The same six Parts in English, as LOINC's Part.csv
                      displays them (PartDisplayName), and LOINC's
                      ConsumerName, both verbatim. Not a translation.

zh_CN_names.tsv and zh_CN_parts.tsv.gz are translations of LOINC. Under
section 12 of the LOINC License (5.8), Regenstrief Institute was notified
before the work began, all right, title and interest in a translation of LOINC
is assigned to Regenstrief Institute, Inc. (and to the LOINC Committee for a
translation of the LOINC Table), and the translation is transmitted to
Regenstrief and made available under the LOINC License. en_parts.tsv.gz is
LOINC content as released. All three are therefore distributed under the LOINC
License, not under this project's Apache-2.0 licence. Regenstrief Institute
does not verify the accuracy of translations; none of these files is clinical
advice.

Prepared by the Mirobody project (Theta Health) with the help of language
models, reviewed by automated rules and independent second readers.
